WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.440
We have very big political news to talk about
today.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:10.290
Ohio has decided to switch to an all by mail
Democratic primary, which will run essentially

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.969
from now until April 20th.

00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:14.820
And the idea is a good one.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.620
Republican Governor Mike DeWine in Ohio has
been one of the best governors on the Corona

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.000
virus response.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.400
But there are major concerns about the specifics
of how Ohio is doing this.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.260
And you'll very clearly understand why when
I give you the details for context.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:34.200
Earlier this week, Nancy Pelosi said on MSNBC
that in general, because of the virus, we

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.570
should be switching to mailing in our ballots.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.130
And I completely agree.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.469
Trump doesn't want this.

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:40.950
We know why Trump doesn't want it.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.410
Trump knows that if more people can vote more
easily in November, it's bad for him.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:49.129
It's more likely that he does not get a second
presidential term.

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:50.129
And it's good for Democrats.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.480
So there's this battle where Nancy Pelosi
wants to vote by mail.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.460
Donald Trump does not want vote by mail.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.930
Now, you might remember that the Ohio Democratic
primary was scheduled for Tuesday, March 17th.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.100
That was sort of like Super Tuesday three.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.680
We had Super Tuesday on March 3rd, colloquially,
Super Tuesday 2 on March 10th, and then Super

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.750
Tuesday three on March 17th.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.549
Ohio postponed because of the virus.

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:16.479
The idea was to reschedule to June 2nd.

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:21.220
The new plan is it will be a mail in primary
in Ohio.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:25.270
And voters will have until April twenty eighth
to submit their ballots.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.340
Now, in general, this does sound good.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:33.580
And indeed, Republican Governor Mike DeWine
said he would sign this bill soon and we can

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.119
get started on this vote by mail Democratic
primary.

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.229
But there are some concerns that voters are
going to end up disenfranchised because the

00:01:41.229 --> 00:01:46.600
way that this is likely to work out is the
Ohio secretary of state is going to send out

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:52.670
a postcard to every registered voter and the
postcard will say, hey, we're voting by mail.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.650
You have to request an absentee ballot.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:00.390
And that is really the source of the problem
here, because even if you are a registered

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.750
voter, you won't get a ballot automatically.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:08.320
You'll get a card that tells you how to ask
for a ballot.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.440
Now, the reason for this and this is true,
that the secretary of state says this and

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.700
this is true.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:19.050
The absentee ballot rules, as many of you
know in many states are you have to request

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.780
an absentee ballot.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.760
You can't just send ballots to everybody.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.580
You have to have a process whereby someone
says, I want an absentee ballot and here's

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.580
why.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.580
That's true.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.470
But these are special circumstances.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:34.230
These are unprecedented circumstances.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:38.090
So what should be done is in the Corona virus
bill that's being passed, which includes that

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.400
there's going to be a vote by mail primary.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.000
They should include a provision that changes
the rule.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.730
It suspends the rule and says we're going
to send everybody a ballot instead of a postcard.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:53.150
In other words, decide as a legislature, this
particular circumstance is so unusual and

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.570
so different.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:59.200
We need to suspend the you must request the
ballot rule because otherwise the timeline

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.400
probably won't work.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.690
It's April 2nd today.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.000
That leaves us 26 days for voting.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:11.220
In those 26 days, the state needs to design,
agree upon a design, print and mail postcards

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.190
to every registered voter.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:17.020
Voters then need to in the midst of everything
everybody's dealing with.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:22.050
Send that back or rather go through the process
of asking for a ballot, which according to

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.580
the secretary of state's web site, you have
to print and sign the ballot request form,

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.800
mail it back by snail mail.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.230
Those ballots then need to be sent out.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.959
Feet be filled out.

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:35.849
And again, you have to mail that back.

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:37.520
It's really not reasonable.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.549
And the ACLU and other groups agree this will
disenfranchise people.

00:03:42.549 --> 00:03:44.410
So we need to see how they deal with this.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:50.970
I believe the simplest path is simply suspend
the rule that says you have to request an

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.470
absentee ballot.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:56.069
Say this is such an extenuating circumstance.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.870
We're sending a ballot to everybody.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.020
Now, in terms of the race itself in Ohio,
the latest polling we have out of Ohio is

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.099
from mid-March.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:04.950
Things could have changed since then.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.770
Two polls from mid-March in one of them.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:11.080
Joe Biden is ahead of Bernie by twenty three
in another mid-March poll.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.220
Joe Biden is ahead of Bernie by 22.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.340
It's been two weeks of virus craziness.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:20.079
It's conceivable that those numbers may have
changed to some degree.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:21.079
We don't know.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:23.400
But that is the latest out of Ohio.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:28.630
And we will let you know probably by Monday
there if there's no advancement on this by.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.580
One day we know it simply is not going to
work.

